  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "Given that \n\n$$\n\\frac{x-4}{(x-2)^{2}}=\\frac{A}{x-2}-\\frac{2}{(x-2)^{2}},\n$$\n\nwhat is the value of $A?$",
  "worked_solution": "Multiplying both sides of the given equality by $(x-2)^{2}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-4 & =A(x-2)-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=0$  gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0-4 & =A(0-2)-2 \\\\ -4 & =-2A-2 \\\\ 2A & =2 \\\\ A & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
